            <ArticleTitle>Bilateral testicular pain due to masturbation interruptus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>382-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case is reported of a young man with apparent idiopathic pain in the testicles, inguinal regions, and perineum. An unusual cause and mechanism were found. A personality of antisex attitudes with a sense of guilt and sex-suppressive tendencies was observed. These were the underlying but indirect factors in the causation of pain exposed only on inquiry into his personal habits; otherwise the pain most likely would have been labelled as &quot;functional&quot; or psychologic.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
